{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Manage the Node.js application as infraset-nodejs.service.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The named systemd unit was validated, enabled, active, and running the Node.js process under its dedicated service account.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ed728de390d54d9c","cmd-fb12bc3523df4aa8","cmd-85380004ad5d43b1"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Have the Node.js application listen only on loopback port 3000.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Socket inspection showed the Node.js process listening at 127.0.0.1:3000; its loopback endpoint returned the expected response, while connection to node1's managed IP on port 3000 was refused.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5587eebca7c14623","cmd-f3c54b829732479a","cmd-85380004ad5d43b1"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Configure HAProxy on node1 to serve HTTP on port 80 and forward root-path traffic to the Node.js backend.","status":"satisfied","summary":"HAProxy's validated configuration binds port 80 and selects 127.0.0.1:3000 as its default backend. The service was enabled and active, HAProxy was directly observed listening on *:80, and a request through node1's port 80 succeeded.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5f764ebc103b4c56","cmd-219d372c77fd40dd","cmd-77979cc3e786410a","cmd-85380004ad5d43b1"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Return HTTP 200 with the exact body infraset-nodejs from the root endpoint.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Repeated requests to http://10.100.249.10/ returned HTTP 200 with the exact 15-byte body infraset-nodejs.","evidence_ids":["cmd-77979cc3e786410a","cmd-85380004ad5d43b1"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No executor-caused failed services or package inconsistency was observed. Temporary command artifacts were cleaned up; the added systemd-private directory is normal runtime state for the active, task-required service. The exposed port 80 and loopback-only port 3000 match the contract.","evidence_ids":["global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","cmd-f3c54b829732479a","cmd-85380004ad5d43b1"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied: the application is managed by the required active systemd service, listens only on 127.0.0.1:3000, and is proxied by HAProxy on port 80 with the required HTTP 200 response and exact body.","limitations":["The successful port-80 request originated on node1 using its managed IP rather than from an independent external client.","The lifecycle socket inventory was empty, so socket conclusions rely on the captured executor ss and curl observations."]}
